  "body": "PRE-MERGE VERIFICATION COMPLETE; actual-merge replay and durable receipt remain required for closure.\n\nProspective registration e36486f067349ce42083ff17f7972c9d86e9fffd is a direct child of verified parent278be101e2c3c9e1cc4745533be94b306967bdf1. Reviewed execution sourcea66311a7b28d5eb452d50b8bfa5f0a2904f967cd; publication head9c650ae56d14eb2ea12f608637c7edd79ff22539.\n\nMathematical result: all admitted no-unary rooted trees with exactly two internal vertices and k>=2 admit paths of total L1 profile deviation at most1. Hence B1=Binf=Bs=1 between distinct exact components; LEX remains a separate objective. Universal unit barriers and the three-or-more-internal-vertex obstruction class remain unresolved.\n\nRun36801762616 passes531 checks (475 inherited+56 new), substantive RED controls, complete12-graph enumeration, and fresh inherited science. Finite totals:1322896states,11558358edges,59profiles,156canonical representative normalizations,722component pairs,0construction failures and0nonunit pairs. Independent source/evidence review accepted the construction and implementation; final publication review required before exact-head merge.\n\nFresh publication reproduction passed all531 checks and all18scientific files match byte-for-byte. Root audit verified59execution manifest members,1460source/inputGitblobs,158publication members, full API ZIP chunk reconstruction and unchanged source tree. Science artifact11135749219 SHA256 ebcf76471d428cbcea3cc2028079e30dc80c044eac80ae4d1c0ce4c499c9f2da; publication artifact11136324437 SHA256 da2dad3a45a56b2cf4a73b4b34bfc2a2d04fd367f8a651dfa31c5c72a278cec1.\n\nDisclosed failed attempt: run36800975231 at3d7a62d91f2a99a03446e325244229afcb53f820 passed scientific checks but packaging rejected an extra trailing protocol LF (4478versus4477bytes). The exact original preregistration blob fd91b68bb11e449d15e883d14233b8d87e02dc67 was restored; strict equality now also runs before science. No scientific/model/domain/proof/acceptance changes. Full failed artifact11135692601, metadata and logs are durably preserved in evidence/prior_failure; its scientific bytes equal the clean rerun. No retrospective preregistration or certification of the failed run is claimed.",
